  data: {
    LLM: 'Play tight: start with hands that have a deuce and a seven, or three cards to an eight that don’t make a straight. Never draw to hands that can make a straight. A-2-3-4-5 is bad (ace is high). Best hand is 7-5-4-3-2 offsuit.\n\nPosition matters: act last when possible to see opponents’ draw sizes. Be aggressive—bet and raise more than you check and call. From early position raise only with strong two-card draws (e.g. 2-3-4, 2-3-7); loosen in late position.\n\nSnowing: in position, stand pat with weak hands when opponents have drawn many cards to pressure them. On the final draw, jack-high is slightly favoured over a one-card draw; adjust by position. Avoid drawing to nine-lows when inexperienced.',
